UPDATE companies SET description='Boston Electronics operates from Brookline, Massachusetts, where it has served the electro-optics market for four decades. No individual founders are named in the available records.

The company distributes advanced electro-optical components and specialized systems for microscopy and research. Its portfolio spans photon-counting modules, ultraviolet and infrared detectors, quantum cascade lasers, terahertz sources and imagers, and laboratory instrumentation such as blackbody calibration sources and laser power sensors. Boston Electronics maintains a web store with filtering tools for product selection and provides application engineering support to help customers integrate these components into their own designs.

Customers come from environmental monitoring, process control, scientific instrumentation, life sciences and biomedical technology, building and home automation, and security and surveillance. The company also supports academic and government research programs, including collaborations with organizations such as MIT''s Advanced LIGO group and the Society for Neuroscience.

Boston Electronics states that its purpose is to enable customers to develop superior products and perform leading-edge research by supplying a broad range of advanced electro-optical solutions backed by knowledgeable application support. It emphasizes long-standing relationships with specialized manufacturers worldwide to bring advantaged, high-performance products to market.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Distribution of electro-optical components and systems", "Application engineering and technical support", "Calibration services (via partner sglux)", "Web-based product selection and ordering", "Photon counting system integration (TCSPC/FLIM/LIDAR)", "UV, IR, and THz detector and source procurement", "Quantum cascade laser (QCL) system supply", "Infrared imaging array and camera sourcing", "Terahertz source, detector, and imager procurement", "Laboratory instrumentation supply (blackbodies, beam profilers, power sensors)"], "industries": ["Environmental monitoring", "Process control", "Scientific instrumentation", "Life sciences and biomedical technologies", "Building and home automation", "Security and surveillance", "Academic and government research", "Microscopy", "Atmospheric studies (DIAL LIDAR)"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Indium Gallium Arsenide (InGaAs)", "Indium Arsenide Antimonide (InAsSb)", "Indium Arsenide (InAs)", "Type-II Superlattice (T2SLS)", "Quantum Cascade Laser semiconductor materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Four decades of specialization in photo-detection and photon generation", "Knowledgeable application support for component selection and system integration", "Broad portfolio sourced from leading global electro-optics manufacturers", "Web store with product filtering and navigation for easy procurement", "Partnerships with niche suppliers such as sglux, Becker & Hickl, and Alpes Lasers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Brookline, Ma