UPDATE companies SET description='Cadillac Products Automotive Company (CPAC) is headquartered in Troy, Michigan, with additional plants in Rogers City and Roseville, Michigan, and Schertz, Texas. The business traces its roots to 1942, when M.P. Williams founded Cadillac Bag Company to fulfill a World War II defense packaging program for Chrysler. Now in its fourth generation of family ownership and management, the company has evolved from a packaging supplier into a plastics-converting specialist for the automotive sector.

CPAC designs, develops, and manufactures protective plastic parts, exterior and interior acoustical components, and door water shields. Its integrated operations cover cast and blown film extrusion, robotic adhesive application, custom injection molding, thermoforming and cold forming, die and water-jet cutting, assembly of pads and fibers, and in-house testing. The company employs approximately 225 people across its facilities and reports annual sales exceeding $50 million.

The primary customer base is the automotive industry, including General Motors, Ford, Stellantis (formerly FCA), Nissan, and tier-one suppliers such as Magna. CPAC has also applied its converting expertise to medical gown manufacturing through its ProTEC-USA division.

The company emphasizes a “one-stop-shop” model, keeping all processes under one roof and producing 100% American-made products from start to finish. Its in-house prototyping capability can verify proof-of-concept in days, and its quality systems are certified to IATF 16949 and ISO 14001 across multiple sites.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 14001:2015','ISO 45001:2018']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cast film extrusion", "Blown film extrusion", "Robotic adhesive application", "In-house prototyping and design", "Custom injection molding", "Assembly of pads, fibers, and foams", "Thermoforming", "Cold forming", "Steel rule die cutting", "Water jet cutting", "In-house testing (third-party certified lab)", "FIBERSORB AC (thermoset resin impregnated fiber mat)", "FIBERSORB WL (synthetic shoddy fiber mat for wheel liners)", "Molded fiber (PET or shoddy fibers)", "FIBERSORB ACB (synthetic shoddy fiber mat <130\u00b0C)", "SOUNDLOC (filled EVA acoustic resin)", "Die cutting (flat PET, PP, cotton shoddy fiber)", "FIBERSORB GL (thermoset impregnated fiber mat with glass fiber)", "SOUNDLOC-Seal (EVA barrier with fiber decoupler, patented seal technology)", "Thin wall hybrid molding (variable thickness injection molding)", "FIBERSORB NF (impregnated mat with natural fibers)", "CONTROL FLOW-SL (dissipative multi-layer acoustical product)", "Polyethylene extrusion (air, dust, moisture barrier)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical"], "materials": ["Plastic resin pellets", "EVA (ethylene vinyl acetate)", "PET (polyethylene terephthalate)", "PP (polypropylene)", "Cotton shoddy fiber", "Synthetic shoddy fiber", "Glass fiber", "Natural fibers", "Polyethylene", "Thermoset resin"], "equipment": ["Polyethylene cast film extruder (Fabricon)", "Injection molding machines", "Robotic adhesive dispensing tools", "Water jet cutting robots", "Automation robotics"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American-made from start to finish", "Al