UPDATE companies SET description='Cal Manufacturing operates from Vicksburg, Michigan, where it has served the resistance welding industry for over half a century. The company is woman-owned and functions as a division of CAL Manufacturing, Inc., though the founding year and original founders are not publicly disclosed.

The company manufactures a range of resistance welding products including air-cooled and water-cooled jumpers, dual-conductor "Kickless" cables, the patented Swivel King kickless cable, induction furnace cables, and copper laminated shunts. It also provides cable repair and rebuilding services, recycling, and custom cable design supported by CNC machining for adapters, busbars, and water-cooled cable adapters. Facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not published.

Primary customers include automotive OEMs, Tier I, II, and III suppliers, and distributors, with a noted presence in Mexico for export to the automotive sector. The company also serves the robotics welding market, supplying industrial cable management for robotic spot welders and resistance welders.

Cal Manufacturing differentiates itself with expedited shipping programs offering same-day or next-day delivery on most stocked items, a cable repair and rebuilding service, the ability to cross-reference competitor part numbers, and a patented Swivel King cable that allows weld heads to twist 180 degrees with minimal force. The company emphasizes quality inspection on every product and adherence to automotive quality standards.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman-owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Resistance welding cable manufacturing", "Cable repair and rebuilding", "Recycling services", "CNC machining", "Custom cable design", "Copper laminated shunt manufacturing", "Electrode design and production", "Industrial cable management", "Robotic cable management", "Swivel King cable production", "Expedited shipping", "Cross-referencing competitor parts", "Reconditioned parts supply"], "industries": ["Resistance welding", "Automotive (OEM, Tier I, II, III)", "Robotics welding", "Industrial manufacturing", "Distribution"], "materials": ["Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same day or next day for most products; expedited same-day or two-day shipping available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day or next-day shipping on most stocked products", "Expedited delivery programs for same-day or two-day shipping", "Cable repair and rebuilding service with recycling", "Patented Swivel King cable for robotic welding applications", "Cross-referencing of competitor part numbers"], "facts_used": ["Location: Vicksburg, MI -> db", "Woman-owned certification -> db", "Over 50 years experience in resistance welding -> /", "Products: air-cooled jumpers, water-cooled jumpers, dual-conductor kickless cables, Swivel King, induction furnace cables, copper laminated shunts -> /", "Services: cable repair and rebuilding, recycling, custom cable design, CNC machining -> /", "Industries: automotive OEMs, Tier I/II/III, distributors, robotics welding -> /", "Expedited shipping: same-day/next-day, two-day programs -> /", "Patented Swivel King cable -> /", "Cross-referencing competitor part numbers -> /", "Quality inspection and automotive standards -> /", "Presence in Mexico for export -> /", "Key personnel: Russ Hayward (Plant Manager), Cheryl Benson (Board of Trustees) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cal Manufacturing, Inc., is growing to be your complete supplier for all cable needs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["Export to Mexico for automotive OEMs, distributors, and Tier I, II, III suppliers"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cal-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Calgreg Electronics operates from Warwick, Rhode Island, where it was founded by Robert Mazzeo. The company began with a focus on providing the electronics industry with rapid electrical and mechanical engineering support through a distribution partner that could manage inventory and deliver a broad range of value-added services.

The firm distributes electronic and electromechanical components, electronic packaging products, and related hardware such as interconnects, thermal management solutions, wedge-loks, rugged card guides, enclosures, and enclosure hardware. Beyond distribution, Calgreg offers vendor-managed inventory, electrical and mechanical design, electrical testing, thermal management design and testing, supply chain management leveraging an Asian supplier network, and assembly services.

Its customer base consists of electronics manufacturers and other companies requiring quick-turn engineering support and supply-chain management for electromechanical components. The company positions itself as a partner for businesses that need both product availability and technical expertise in areas such as thermal management and electrical design.

