UPDATE companies SET description='California Solar Electric Cooperative operates from Grass Valley, California, as the state''s first worker-owned solar cooperative. The company is structured as a cooperative owned by its worker-owners, who collectively manage design, installation, and service operations. While a specific founding year is not disclosed, the team cites two decades of experience in solar system design and installation.

The cooperative designs and installs integrated solar photovoltaic systems paired with battery storage, as well as backup generators, electric-vehicle chargers, and smart energy management platforms. It also provides ongoing service and repair, including system monitoring through manufacturer platforms such as Enphase, SMA, SolarEdge, and SunPower. Service agreements guarantee a response and appointment within two business days and a 15 percent discount on billable labor and materials for corrective maintenance.

Customers span residential homeowners, commercial businesses, non-profit organizations, and government agencies throughout the region.

