UPDATE companies SET description='Cameron Manufacturing & Design traces its roots to 1983 when Frank LaViola Sr. founded a fabrication shop in Horseheads, New York, to address a regional need for custom metalwork. The company expanded to a second facility in Orlando, Florida, adding 28,000 square feet to the original 145,000-square-foot New York plant. In 2007, LaViola transitioned ownership to an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP), making the workforce of hundreds of skilled employees the company’s owners.

Today Cameron operates as a full-service metal manufacturer, offering custom sheet metal fabrication, CNC machining (milling, lathing, waterjet and laser cutting), welding (including rolling, bending, punching, heavy fabrication, CWI-certified and sanitary welding), metal finishing (powder coating, painting, vibratory tumbling), engineering design, project management, and on-site installation.

The company serves food and dairy processors requiring USDA- and 3A-compliant equipment, rail and transit agencies needing custom metal components and signaling systems, and transportation equipment manufacturers. Its customer base spans Fortune 500 corporations and smaller regional firms across the United States.

Cameron emphasizes turnkey delivery — from CAD design through fabrication, machining, welding, finishing, and installation — backed by ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 certifications at its New York facility. The employee-owned structure is cited as a driver of quality workmanship, on-time delivery, and responsive service.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','USDA compliance','3A Industrial Standards compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication", "CNC machining", "CNC lathing", "CNC milling", "Waterjet cutting", "Laser cutting", "Powder coating", "Painting", "Vibratory tumbling", "Rolling", "Bending", "Punching", "Heavy fabrication", "Heavy welding", "CWI (Certified Welding Inspector) services", "Custom sanitary welding", "Engineering design services", "Equipment installation services", "Project management", "Metal forming", "Assembly", "On-site installation", "Start-up support"], "industries": ["Food & dairy", "Beverage", "Pet food", "Rail & transit", "Transportation equipment", "General manufacturing"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Inconel", "Monel", "Hastelloy", "Nickel"], "equipment": ["Amada Punch/Laser LC-2012 C1 NT", "Amada Fiber laser", "CNC machining centers", "Lathes", "Milling machines", "Waterjet cutting equipment", "Laser cutting equipment", "Powder coating equipment", "Painting equipment", "Vibratory tumbler", "Forming equipment", "Welders", "Finishing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2007", "Turnkey solutions from design through on-site installation", "ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 certified at Horseheads, NY facility", "USDA and 3A Industrial Standards compliance for food and dairy equipment", "Multi-disciplinary capabilities under one roof: fabrication, machining, welding, finishing, engineering"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 by Frank LaViola Sr. -> /about-us", "Employee-owned since 2007 (ESOP) -> /about-us", "Two locations: Hors