UPDATE companies SET description='Campo Sheet Metal Works, Inc. was founded in 1926 by Salvatore Campo in Houston, Texas. What began as a garage operation fabricating gutters and flashing has grown into one of Houston’s custom metal fabrication facilities. The company remains family-owned and operated, with the fourth generation of the Campo family now part of the team.

The shop provides a full range of metal fabrication services, including water jet cutting, press brake forming, plate rolling, plasma and oxyfuel cutting, shearing, structural rolling, punching, drilling, sawing, and welding. Equipment includes three CNC water jets, multiple press brakes, turret punches, plate and structural rolls, saws, drill presses, and a robotic welding cell for consistent repeat welds. The facility operates as a one-stop shop, handling design assistance through turnkey fabrication.

Campo serves industrial and manufacturing markets such as oil and gas, aerospace, petrochemical, architectural, food and beverage plants, material handling, and marine.

