UPDATE companies SET description='Campofrio Food Group America operates from South Chesterfield, Virginia, as the U.S. arm of Sigma Foods, a multinational food company owned by the Mexican conglomerate ALFA. The business produces, markets, and distributes a wide range of refrigerated and cured meats, dairy items, and other food products across Mexico, Europe, the United States, and Latin America.

Its portfolio encompasses over 100 brands worldwide, with 16 brands each generating more than US$100 million in net sales. Core operations include meat processing, curing, dairy production, and large-scale distribution supported by a resilient supply chain.

Its U.S. presence was strengthened in April 2026 with the acquisition of Roger Wood, a move that expanded its brand portfolio in the American market.

Differentiation centers on consumer-driven innovation. Sigma Foods operates "The Studio," a global excellence center for design and innovation, and runs "Tastech by Sigma," an open-innovation program that has evaluated more than 2,850 startups and executed 59 pilots across nine countries with a network of over 200 global partners. These capabilities enable rapid development of new products aligned with evolving consumer preferences.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Meat processing and curing", "Dairy product manufacturing", "Food product innovation and R&D", "Global supply chain and distribution", "Brand portfolio management", "Open innovation collaboration"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Meat processing", "Dairy processing", "Consumer packaged goods", "Food distribution"], "materials": ["Cold meats", "Cured meats", "Dairy products"], "equipment": [], "volume": "1.8 million tons of food sold annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global innovation center \"The Studio\" for consumer-centric product design", "Open innovation program Tastech with 2,850+ startups analyzed and 59 pilots executed", "66 manufacturing plants across 17 countries providing resilient supply chain", "Portfolio of 100+ brands including 16 with annual net sales exceeding US$100 million", "Strategic acquisition of Roger Wood (2026) strengthening U.S. market position"], "facts_used": ["South Chesterfield, Virginia headquarters -> db", "Part of Sigma Foods (ALFA) -> /", "Produces cold meats, cured meats, dairy -> /", "66 plants, 17 countries, 48,000+ employees, $9.273B revenue -> /", "1.8 million tons food sold annually -> /", "Over 100 brands, 16 with >$100M sales -> /", "Innovation center ''The Studio'' -> /", "Tastech program: 2,850+ startups, 59 pilots, 200+ allies -> /", "Acquired Roger Wood April 2026 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "produce, comercializa y distribuye carnes fr\u00edas,