UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Foods was founded in 1934 in Charlotte, North Carolina, and has operated continuously as a maker of sweet baked goods for over 90 years. The company maintains its headquarters in Charlotte and runs a modern baking facility in nearby Pineville, NC.

The company produces a range of sweet baked goods including gem donuts, donut sticks, honey buns, fritters, cinnamon rolls, and mini pies under its Duchess brand and as a private-label and co-manufacturing partner. All products are made from scratch using time-honored techniques combined with technology; the Pineville plant features automated packaging from Schubert and was named Food Engineering’s 2025 Plant of the Year.

Customers include retailers across convenience, grocery, mass-market, and club channels, as well as quick-serve and hospitality food-service operators. The company positions itself as a bakery partner of choice for brands seeking customized sweet baked goods and scalable co-manufacturing solutions.

Carolina Foods traces its differentiation to early innovations—it claims to be the first to crack extended shelf life for sweet baked goods and the first to introduce the honey bun—and to its in-house control of every production step, which it says enables faster innovation, gold-standard quality and safety 365 days a year, and unmatched service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Scratch baking", "Extended shelf life formulation", "Co-manufacturing", "Private label production", "Retail distribution", "Food service supply", "Automated packaging (Schubert system)", "Product innovation and development", "Quality assurance and food safety", "In-house process control"], "industries": ["Retail", "Food service", "Private label", "Co-manufacturing", "Convenience stores", "Grocery", "Club stores"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Schubert packaging system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First to develop extended shelf life for sweet baked goods", "First to introduce the honey bun", "Award-winning, state-of-the-art bakery facility in Pineville, NC (Food Engineering 2025 Plant of the Year)", "Gold-standard quality, safety, and service 365 days a year", "In-house control of every production step for faster innovation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1934 -> db", "Headquarters Charlotte, NC -> db", "Pineville, NC facility -> /", "Products: gem donuts, donut sticks, honey buns, fritters, cinnamon rolls, mini pies -> /", "Made from scratch, time-honored techniques, industry-leading technology -> /", "Schubert packaging system -> /about-us", "Food Engineering 2025 Plant of the Year -> /about-us", "Retail channel counts: 21,698 convenience stores, 8,600 value retailers, 4,505 conventional grocers, 3,419 mass-market retailers, 873 club stores -> /about-us", "Channels: retail, private label, co-manufacturing, food service -> /", "First to crack extended shelf life, first honey bun -> /about-us", "Gold standard quality, safety, se