cquisitions: J. Hamelin 2015, Lone Star Reel 2016 -> /about", "Leadership succession: Henry Carris, Bill Carris, Mike Curran, Dave Ferraro, Alberto Aguilar -> /about", "Employee-owned tag explicitly stated -> / and /about", "Founded year 1951 explicitly stated -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "No other reel manufacturer offers a more comprehensive product line.", "founded_year": "1951", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carris-reels-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carson Hi-Tech Inc. was established in 1994 in Carson City, Nevada. The company operates as a plastics injection molding specialist serving a broad range of markets from its single facility in the state capital.

The company runs a 1,300-square-foot facility housing six Van Dorn injection molding machines. It offers a turn-key operation covering mold design, injection molding, and a range of secondary processes including pad printing, hot stamping, sonic welding, assembly, packing and shipping, laser cutting, plastic shadowing, tooling, SLA, and thermoforming.

Carson Hi-Tech serves a diverse set of industries: medical, mining, education, hobby, lawn and garden, custom electronics and electrical, housing, toys, sporting goods, automotive, pets, and photography.

